  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONSERVATION OF THE TIGERS OF GUNUNG LEUSER NATIONAL PARK THROUGH IMPROVED LAW ENFORCEMENT AND REDUCED HUMAN-TIGER CONFLICT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The long term goal is to bring tigers back to their natural carrying capacity in Gunung Leuser National Park (GLNP) and to bring the tiger population of GLNP to a level that is both capable of sustained breeding and compatible with the human activities legally permitted within GLNP. This is to be done through improving and strengthening law enforcement and human-tiger conflict mitigation in the GLNP landscape. The project objectives are to: (1) Protect tiger, tiger prey and tiger habitat, by patrolling the key tiger core area of GLNP; and, (2) Decrease human-tiger conflict, by mitigating human-tiger conflict in key areas of GLNP.</narrative>
  </description>
